by\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534217 17592186045417 true] [17592186414494 1072 #uuid "7b4a741d-30d4-5d2c-9fde-2ae106aac7d2" 13194139534217 17592186045417 true] [17592186414494 1074 "First, we need to convert $P$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $P$ has $4$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $4.$" 13194139534217 17592186045417 true] [17592186414495 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414491 13194139534217 17592186045417 true] [17592186414495 1069 "q-35451" 13194139534217 17592186045417 true] [17592186414495 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534217 17592186045417 true] [17592186414495 1071 "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are the pivot columns of $A?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534217 17592186045417 true] [17592186414495 1072 #uuid "a184c001-bd4f-576e-9731-bffadf7bf486" 13194139534217 17592186045417 true] [17592186414495 1074 "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd, and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534217 17592186045417 true] [17592186414496 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414493 13194139534217 17592186045417 true] [17592186414496 1069 "q-73610" 13194139534217 17592186045417 true] [17592186414496 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534217 17592186045417 true] [17592186414496 1071 "The row echelon form matrix $M$ is given below. What are the pivot columns of $M?$\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534217 17592186045417 true] [17592186414496 1072 #uuid "c6f93be2-7ce6-5b4b-af0d-5674ab7e6429" 13194139534217 17592186045417 true] [17592186414496 1074 "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $M$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $3$rd, and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534217 17592186045417 true] [17592186414497 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414492 13194139534217 17592186045417 true] [17592186414497 1069 "q-73613" 13194139534217 17592186045417 true] [17592186414497 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534217 17592186045417 true] [17592186414497 1071 "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534217 17592186045417 true] [17592186414497 1072 #uuid "ef768962-c254-565f-ad90-7c7187cd37b0" 13194139534217 17592186045417 true] [17592186414497 1074 "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $2$nd column." 13194139534217 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0bf2fc69-40c7-50e